<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Nodejs on Tech and Lifestyle Blog</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/tags/nodejs/</link><description>Recent content in Nodejs on Tech and Lifestyle Blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2025 Yalchin Mammadli</copyright><lastBuildDate>Tue, 13 May 2025 00:53:10 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/tags/nodejs/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>How to Deploy Nodejs App</title><link>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/how-to-deploy-nodejs-app/</link><pubDate>Tue, 13 May 2025 00:53:10 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/how-to-deploy-nodejs-app/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;In this tutorial, we will be deploying a simple URL shortener API built-in express framework of NodeJs. It is pretty simple, uses MongoDB as its database, and you can find its source code &lt;a
href="https://github.com/Yalchin403/express-urlshortener-api"
target="_blank"
&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a VPS, I use a Linode ubuntu server, and I assume that you have at least some basic knowledge when it comes to Linux.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class="relative group"&gt;Install Node and NPM
&lt;div id="install-node-and-npm" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#install-node-and-npm" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;curl -sL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_12.x &lt;span class="p"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; sudo -E bash -
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sudo apt install nodejs
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# verify that bash is installed&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;node --version
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 class="relative group"&gt;Clone your Repo
&lt;div id="clone-your-repo" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#clone-your-repo" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone [link to your github repo]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/how-to-deploy-nodejs-app/featured.png"/></item></channel></rss>